---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/guides/implementation-plan";
const title = "Shopify email implementation plan";
const desc = "Launch by dependency and evidence for Shopify lifecycle email with explicit owners, proposed exercises and reversible decisions.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "How long should implementation take?",
    "answer": "Estimate from integration, permission and workflow dependencies. Use acceptance gates and staffing capacity rather than a vendor-wide speed promise."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should all flows launch together?",
    "answer": "Choose independently observable releases. Additional flows need their own contract and overlap review before enrollment."
  },
  {
    "question": "What proves readiness?",
    "answer": "Retain evidence for eligibility, queue cancellation, content, permissions and rollback. Revenue dashboards alone cannot demonstrate those behaviors."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/guides">Operator guides</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Launch by dependency and evidence</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Launch by dependency and evidence for Shopify lifecycle email with explicit owners, proposed exercises and reversible decisions.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Define the first useful release</h2><p>Pick a customer problem and a bounded audience, such as product education after fulfillment or a promised signup benefit. Specify the expected message, exclusions and responsible owner. Do not select flow count or a calendar week as the definition of success. Keep existing essential order notifications owned and observable.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Assign access and operating authority</h2><p>Name who can change Shopify settings, sending configuration, offers, permission mappings and integrations. Give an internal owner authority to pause a branch and resolve supplier questions. Record escalation contacts and access recovery. An agency handoff is incomplete if the merchant cannot make and reverse an ordinary exclusion change.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Map the data contract</h2><p>For customer, order, checkout, product variant and fulfillment data, document source identifiers, timestamps, update semantics and missing-field behavior. Distinguish event time from receipt time. Ask the connector owner how history and live events interact so a historical import cannot silently enroll customers in a new live journey.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Build permission and sending foundations</h2><p>Map channel and purpose permissions and suppressed states before enrolling audiences. Verify sender configuration with the provider and inspect representative message headers. Check unsubscribe behavior through connected tools. Use the consent and deliverability guides for their separate reviews; authentication alone does not establish permission or inbox placement.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Design a workflow contract</h2><p>Write the trigger, branch conditions, delays, offer promise, exit rules and dispatch-time exclusions in plain language. Include purchase during delay, cancellation, refund, support hold and unavailable inventory. Design transactional and promotional content separately. Use the collision matrix before adding any second sender with overlapping eligibility.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Sequence by dependencies</h2><p>Start with the bounded workflow whose data and ownership are ready. Add welcome, cart or post-purchase according to the actual customer problem; replenishment needs credible timing inputs and subscription state. Browse and winback should wait if their identity or eligibility is uncertain. There is no mandatory flow order based on SKU count or monthly orders.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Proposed acceptance exercise</h2><p>Use isolated test profiles and non-sending paths first. Compare expected and actual decisions for new signup, purchase during a queued reminder, withdrawal, gift purchase and repeated event. Then, where authorized, inspect controlled messages for links, rendering, currency, variant and unsubscribe behavior. Record failures honestly; this guide reports no performed tests.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Release with an observable boundary</h2><p>Write the audience boundary, current queue size, rollback command and monitoring owner before enabling sends. Avoid allowing old and new equivalents to send to the same journey. Stop expansion when permission, duplicate-send or integration errors remain unresolved. Choose observation length around event delays and available evidence rather than a fixed trial duration.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Budget and define measurement</h2><p>Separate recurring platform and connector charges from setup, template work, operator time and ongoing maintenance. Finance should record currency, billing period, taxable amounts and included usage for any quote. Establish flow definitions, attribution windows and refund handling before comparing reports. Attributed sales are not automatically incremental profit.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Hand over the operating runbook</h2><p>Have the internal operator change a suppression rule, preview its audience and restore the previous version. Retain the workflow contract, message versions, test record, source mappings and pause instructions. Review incidents and changes with named owners. Schedule the next release only after unresolved defects in its dependencies are closed.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12 prose-shopify"><h2>Integration evidence to request</h2><p>For a custom webhook integration, Shopify documents delivery verification and duplicate handling. Ask the integration owner to show how those controls connect to journey state; webhook verification alone does not establish permission to send.</p><p><a class="link" href="https://shopify.dev/docs/apps/build/webhooks/verify-deliveries">Shopify: verify webhook deliveries</a> (reviewed 25 November 2026).</p></section>
  <nav class="container pb-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4" aria-label="Related operating guidance">
    <a class="link" href="/guides/consent-compliance">Consent compliance</a>
    <a class="link" href="/guides/deliverability">Deliverability</a>
    <a class="link" href="/guides/discount-discipline">Discount discipline</a>
    <a class="link" href="/guides/revenue-attribution">Revenue attribution</a>
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">Use-case playbooks</a>
    <a class="link" href="/for">Store-type guides</a>
  </nav>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
